Subject: [PATCH] Keep the link on D7 media tokens carrying an external_url

D7 media tokens could carry an external_url, which rendered the media as
a link -- typically an image thumbnail linking to the PDF it illustrates
(fact sheets, reports, flyers). The token-to-drupal-media conversion
never read that key, so the image migrated and the link it wrapped was
dropped silently: the page still looks right while the download is gone.
2,702 tokens across 1,075 text rows are affected.

Wrap the generated embed in an anchor when the token has one. The href
keeps its D7 value deliberately -- cas_legacy_file_paths runs after this
step and rewrites quoted hrefs to the D10 files path.
---
--- a/src/OsuMediaEmbed.php
+++ b/src/OsuMediaEmbed.php
@@ -118,7 +118,26 @@
             }
           }
         }
-        return $this->getEmbedCode($embed_metadata) ?? $matches[0];
+        $embed_code = $this->getEmbedCode($embed_metadata);
+        if ($embed_code === NULL) {
+          return $matches[0];
+        }
+
+        // CAS: a D7 media token could carry an external_url, which rendered
+        // the media as a link -- typically an image thumbnail linking to the
+        // PDF it illustrates. 2,702 tokens across 1,075 text rows use it.
+        // Without this the image survives and the link it wrapped is dropped
+        // silently, so the page still looks right while the download is
+        // gone. The href keeps its D7 value on purpose: cas_legacy_file_paths
+        // runs after this step and rewrites quoted hrefs to the D10 files
+        // path. Other token fields are booleans when unset, hence the string
+        // check.
+        $external_url = $tag_info['fields']['external_url'] ?? NULL;
+        if (is_string($external_url) && trim($external_url) !== '') {
+          return '<a href="' . htmlspecialchars(trim($external_url), ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8') . '">'
+            . $embed_code . '</a>';
+        }
+        return $embed_code;
       }
       catch (NotEncodableValueException $e) {
         return $matches[0];
